data: {"id":"gen-1793850117-5HUeJjIcUSpKXJYRiLfE","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1793850117,"model":"dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free","provider":"AtlasCloud","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":", \"new_string\": \"### WHEN TO PROCEED\\n\\nContinue conservatively when the user is unsure, preserve the unsupported\\nrequirement as unknown, and wait only at the review or confirmation boundary.\\n\\n### BRIEF REQUEST + OBVIOUS GAP PATTERN\\n\\nWhen the user gives a short/imperative request (e.g. \\\"根据岗位改简历\\\",\\n\\\"岗位：Python 必须，资料：只写 Excel/R\\\") and the Profile has an obvious,\\nmaterial gap against the target Job, do NOT proceed to generate a proposal.\\nInstead, in one pass:\\n\\n1. Read Profile + Job + source Resume (already loaded or fetched once).\\n2. Produce a **concise gap summary**: which requirement(s) are uncovered,\\n   what evidence exists (if any), and why the gap blocks tailoring.\\n3. Ask **one** highest-value question that can close the gap — use the\\n   `max_fit` question format from GUIDED CLARIFICATION AND WRITING.\\n4. Stop. Do not loop on `career_context_retrieve` with the same query;\\n   if the tool returns the same unsupported-claims list twice, the answer\\n   is \\\"no confirmed evidence\\\" — move to the question.\\n\\nThis pattern fires when the user's request is brief AND the gap is obvious\\nfrom the first Profile read. It supersedes the normal \\\"ask 0–1 questions\\\"\\nguidance because the gap is material and the user has not yet seen it.\""}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}

