data: {"id":"gen-1793850203-gsEfyhjC44l5UhJsQOk4","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1793850203,"model":"dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview:free","provider":"AtlasCloud","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":null,"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":", \"content\": \"---\\nname: evidence-gap-early-surfacing\\ndescription: Ask one question when evidence gaps are obvious instead of looping on retrieval.\\nversion: 1.0.0\\nauthor: Hermes Agent\\nlicense: Project-local\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    category: career\\n    tags: [gap-detection, interaction-efficiency, fact-safety, early-surfacing]\\n    related_skills: [resume-tailoring, job-fit-analysis]\\n---\\n\\n# Evidence gap early surfacing\\n\\n## WHEN TO USE\\n\\nUse when a user gives a short/imperative request to produce or tailor a\\ncareer artifact (resume, fit analysis, profile) AND the first read of the\\navailable evidence (Profile, source Resume, target Job) reveals an obvious,\\nmaterial gap — a requirement the evidence cannot support.\\n\\nThis skill governs the *interaction pattern*, not the domain logic. The\\ndomain skills (resume-tailoring, job-fit-analysis, etc.) still own the\\nfact-safety rules, tailoring modes, and output contracts.\\n\\n## THE PATTERN\\n\\n### Detect\\n\\nAfter reading the Profile, source Resume, and target Job/JD once, check:\\n- Is there a **must-have** requirement with zero confirmed evidence?\\n- Is there a **keyword** in the JD that appears nowhere in the Profile or\\n  source Resume?\\n- Would the first draft of the artifact require inventing a claim?\\n\\nIf the answer to any of these is yes, the gap is material and obvious.\\n\\n### Act — in one pass, no looping\\n\\n1. **State the gap concisely.** Name the requirement, what evidence exists\\n   (if any), and why it blocks the task. 3–5 sentences max.\\n2. **Ask one highest-value question** that can close the gap. Use the\\n   domain skill's question format (e.g. `max_fit` options: 实际做过 /\\n   能够独立完成基础任务 / 接触学习过 / 没有使用过 / 不确定 / 跳过).\\n3. **Stop.** Do not call the same retrieval tool again with the same query.\\n   If the tool returns the same unsupported-claims list twice, the answer\\n   is \\\"no confirmed evidence\\\" — move to the question.\\n\\n### What NOT to do\\n\\n- Do **not** loop on `career_context_retrieve` with minor query variations\\n  hoping to surface evidence that isn't there. The tool is correct; the\\n  evidence isn't.\\n- Do **not** call `career_job_list` repeatedly to re-discover the same\\n  jobs. If the job list hasn't changed, the answer hasn't either.\\n- Do **not** generate a proposal that stuffs a missing keyword or invents\\n  a skill. That is a fact-safety violation, not a workaround.\\n- Do **not** ask more than one question before the user responds. The\\n  user's brief request implies they want forward progress, not an\\n  interrogation.\\n\\n### When this pattern does NOT fire\\n\\n- The gap is minor or optional (preferred-but-not-required).\\n- The evidence is ambiguous and a single retrieval could clarify it.\\n- The user has already been asked this question in a prior turn.\\n- The user explicitly said \\\"don't ask, just generate\\\" or equivalent.\\n\\nIn those cases, fall through to the domain skill's normal workflow.\\n\\n## TOOL DISCIPLINE\\n\\n- Read Profile + Job + Resume **once** at the start.\\n- If a gap is obvious from that read, **stop retrieving** and surface it.\\n- Each additional `career_context_retrieve` call with the same core query\\n  that returns the same unsupported-claims list is a **wasted turn** —\\n  the evidence graph is stable; re-querying it does not make evidence\\n  appear.\\n- The exception: if the Profile or Job was updated between reads (check\\n  `updatedAt`), re-read before concluding.\\n\\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\\n\\nGap summary (concise):\\n- Requirement: <name/ID>\\n- Evidence available: <what exists, or \\\"none\\\">\\n- Why it blocks: <one sentence>\\n- Question: <one question, using domain skill's option format>\\n\\nThen stop. Wait for the user's answer before proceeding to proposal.\""}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}

